{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he approached him, etc. … let your servant speak a word in the ears of my lord.</b> Let my words enter your ears." "<b>And let your anger not burn.</b> From here you learn that he spoke to him harshly." "<b>For you are like Pharaoh.</b> You are regarded in my eyes as a king — this is its plain sense. And its midrash: in the end you will be stricken for it with tzara'at, as Pharaoh was stricken on account of my elderly mother Sarah, for one night that he detained her (Bereshit Rabbah). Another matter: just as Pharaoh decrees and does not fulfill, promises and does not do — so too you; is this what you meant by setting an eye, when you said to set your eye on him? Another matter — for you are like Pharaoh: if you provoke me, I will kill you and your master (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:30.944635471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}